<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh May crude output rises to 2.263 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>Kazakh May crude output rises to 2.263 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakhstan's production of crude oil and gas condensate rose in May to 2.263 million tonnes from 2.134 million tonnes in April, the State Statistics Committee said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The committee released the following figures for energy output in its latest monthly statistical bulletin. (Figures in tonnes, except crude oil in million tonnes and natural gas in</p>
<p>billion cubic meters).</p>
<p> KAZAKH ENERGY OUTPUT	May 97	 Apr 97     Jan-May 97</p>
<p> Crude oil			2.263	  2.134	  10.546</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	 +6.1	   -0.2	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	+18.9	  +16.1	   +15.6</p>
<p> Natural gas		    0.496	  0.655	   3.127</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	-24.3	   -3.5	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	 +1.7	  +17.0	   +14.9</p>
<p> Gasoline		    126,100	 202,200	 674,500</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change     -37.6	   +73.0	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change     -33.9	   -15.3	   -33.4</p>
<p> Diesel			309,500	 251,700     1,150,400</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change     +23.0	   +21.1	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	+4.9	   -17.8	    -11.6</p>
<p> Fuel oil		    230,300	265,200	1,419,500</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change     -13.2	   -9.8		n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change     -19.5	   -5.9	    -10.7</p>
<p>-- Almaty Newsroom +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
